```
This matches the pattern used by `Header.tsx` (`i18n.language ?? "en"`) and all other components in the codebase.

Make the `updatedAt` bump explicit and verify the update affected rows:
```typescript
const updated = await SelectedCalendarRepository.updateManyByCredentialId(
  this.credential.id,
  { updatedAt: new Date() }
);
if (updated.count === 0) {
  logger.warn(`updateManyByCredentialId touched 0 rows for credential ${this.credential.id}`);
}
```
This makes the intent self-documenting and survives any future Prisma `@updatedAt` directive changes.

Destructure `i18n` from `useLocale()` and pass `i18n.language` to `Intl.DateTimeFormat`, with a fallback to match the `Header.tsx` pattern:

```tsx
const { t, i18n } = useLocale();
// ...
{t("cache_last_updated", {
  timestamp: new Intl.DateTimeFormat(i18n.language ?? "en", {
    dateStyle: "short",
    timeStyle: "short",
  }).format(new Date(cacheUpdatedAt)),
  interpolation: { escapeValue: false },
})}
```

This matches the established codebase pattern (`Booker/Header.tsx:94`) and ensures the cache timestamp renders in the user's active locale.
